all creatures. They can't be regenerated.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2023-08-04","toughness":null,"type_line":"Sorcery"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"If you Donate an Aura, it stays where it is, but the targeted player now controls it.","oracle_id":"049d1fb2-cce7-40e7-a633-e84cf9782d89","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Chance for Glory’s first effect affects only creatures you control at the time it resolves. Creatures you begin to control later in the game won’t gain indestructible.","oracle_id":"324af60d-142b-4b6c-afe9-6aa36267d5ee","published_at":"2018-10-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Creatures you control gain indestructible indefinitely. If you find a way to not lose the game during your next turn, they’ll continue to be indestructible for as long as they remain on the battlefield.","oracle_id":"324af60d-142b-4b6c-afe9-6aa36267d5ee","published_at":"2018-10-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you somehow skip the extra turn Chance for Glory gives you or skip that turn’s end step, the delayed triggered ability never triggers.","oracle_id":"324af60d-142b-4b6c-afe9-6aa36267d5ee","published_at":"2018-10-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won't return to the battlefield.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Once the exiled permanent returns, it's considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled permanent will be put into their owners' graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled permanent will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled permanent will cease to exist.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The returned card won't be the target of any spells or abilities that targeted it before. Any spells that don't target, such as Akroma's Vengeance, will still affect it.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"When an effect returns the exiled card \"under your control,\" you control it indefinitely after that. In a multiplayer game, if a player leaves the game, all cards that player owns leave as well. If you leave the game, any creatures you control from Cloudshift's effect are exiled.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"An activated ability has a \"Cost: Effect\" format. Look for the colon. A triggered ability starts with \"when\", \"whenever\", or \"at\".","oracle_id":"b3b00911-ece7-4484-bc36-f211ce72b6cc","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"It can target delayed triggered abilities. For example, a card that says \"Whenever a player cycles a card, you may exile target creature. If you do, return that creature to the battlefield at the beginning of the end step.\" triggers when a player cycles a card and creates a delayed trigger that happens at the beginning of the end step. You can choose to target the \"at the beginning of the end step\" trigger when it is placed on the stack at end of turn.","oracle_id":"b3b00911-ece7-4484-bc36-f211ce72b6cc","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Turn-based actions and special actions like the normal card draw, combat damage, or turning a face-down creature face up can't be targeted.","oracle_id":"b3b00911-ece7-4484-bc36-f211ce72b6cc","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
